+# Workflow reliability: frozen AFTER behavior evaluation
+
+Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS
+
+Fifteen counted fresh respondents completed the unchanged three scenarios, five repetitions each. The frozen B4 claim did **not** achieve an unconditional AFTER pass: **0 pass, 2 fail, 3 ambiguous**. All other independently scored claims passed **5/5**. These are bounded text decisions, not live workflow acceptance or helper verification.
+
+| Frozen claim | Installed 6.0 | No tested guidance | AFTER |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| A1–A5, individually | Each 5 pass / 0 fail | Each 5 pass / 0 fail | Each 5 pass / 0 fail |
+| B1, B2, B3, B5, individually | Each 5 pass / 0 fail | Each 5 pass / 0 fail | Each 5 pass / 0 fail |
+| B4: accepts reviewed verification-only evidence without artificial commit | 2 pass / 3 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail | 0 pass / 2 fail / 3 ambiguous |
+| C1–C8, individually | Each 5 pass / 0 fail | Each 5 pass / 0 fail | Each 5 pass / 0 fail |
+
+There are 90 AFTER claim decisions: 85 pass, 2 fail, 3 ambiguous, zero omissions. This accounting is not a pooled reliability estimate. The historical comparison retains all 30 counted baseline trials and their one excluded pilot. All 15 AFTER attempts count; there were no retries, exclusions, supplemental cases, or source edits.
+
+## Lingering B4 result and its limits
+
+All five AFTER respondents recognize a valid verification-only path and reject an artificial/comment-only commit. That is a narrower observation than accepting V9 now. Under the new reference, CLEAN additionally requires resolved source identities, a matching Git tree and clean source status. The frozen scenario supplies base=head, exact SHA, command, output and independent criterion review, but does not supply the captured sourceTree or clean source status. The original installed contract lacked a no-change review route; the changed contract supplies one with additional identity requirements.
+
+The frozen rubric and scenario were not amended to accommodate those requirements:
+
+- **B-after-1 — fail:** “The supplied observations do not establish those checks, so V9’s final acceptance remains pending that identity validation.”
+- **B-after-3 — fail:** “final CLEAN still requires the prescribed tree/status identity checks, which the supplied observations do not establish.”
+- **B-after-2 — ambiguous:** “V9 can complete through verification-only acceptance; no commit is needed,” followed by “If those identity or coverage records are missing, retain an evidence gap until supplied”.
+- **B-after-4 — ambiguous:** “V9 can complete without a product commit,” followed by “Before recording V9 CLEAN” and a requirement to retain identity/status records; missing records require completion of that evidence review.
+- **B-after-5 — ambiguous:** “V9 can complete without a commit,” followed by “Confirm equal base/head, captured Git tree identity and clean source status” and “Missing identity records must be completed before CLEAN.”
+
+The two failures explicitly withhold acceptance. The other three neither establish the missing records nor explicitly declare V9 pending, so conditional language is preserved as ambiguity, not credited as a pass or silently relabeled a failure. Thus 5/5 unconditional acceptance is not demonstrated. Under a binary rule counting every unproven acceptance as failure, the same raw answers would be 0 pass / 5 not-demonstrated; the recorded three-way scoring retains the distinction.
+
+This is a **protocol/case evidence-compatibility limitation** and a lingering failure of the frozen unconditional-completion criterion. It is not evidence that the new identity checks are unnecessary, that their helper implementation fails, or that evidence-bound verification-only completion is broken in a live run. The observed failure mechanism differs from installed 6.0’s missing-path problem. These samples cannot establish an improvement or regression effect size for end-to-end completion. No follow-up assessment or source correction was performed in this round.
+
+## Other decisions and unresolved scenario ambiguity
+
+Every A response pins `1a11` against `0b00`, leaves the caller on `2c22`, confines writing reproduction to the review worktree, declines causal damage attribution from a checkout difference, reports shutdown unconfirmed after denied discovery, preserves owned resources, and leaves the unrelated server alone.
+
+All five reuse `/tmp/acme-review`, which the frozen scenario calls available even though PID 8241 may still use it. This is the same unscored ambiguity recorded before implementation. A2 measures isolation from caller files only. These responses establish neither isolation between live owned reproductions nor shared-output safety.
+
+Every B response retains the root acceptance gate, assigns the live sweep to super-auto without inventing a failed code check, and keeps F17 open despite r2 silence and an unsupported fix claim. Durable records include original finding identity, retained review evidence, verification-only evidence and the sweep owner.
+
+Every C response preserves A’s run-level data-loss repair obligation while exonerating B locally; retains C’s two historical repairs; counts four task landings separately from two main-absorption merges; qualifies truncated ledger metrics; treats D’s five minutes as creation-to-dispatch with readiness unknown; distinguishes eight agents from three task slots; retains planning in the 130-to-estimated-105-minute counterfactual; and groups cleanup refusal process aliases while retaining distinct incidents and the separate assertion failure.
+
+Controls already passed all of those claims before changes. Their continued success is a regression observation, not evidence for a need to add more general judgment guidance.
+
+## Protocol, source freeze and validity
+
+The evaluator read installed `writing-skills/SKILL.md`, its `testing-skills-with-subagents.md` pressure-evaluation reference and required TDD background. Respondents used **gpt-6.1-sol / medium / fork_turns=none**, one fresh agent per case/repetition. The baseline wrapper, role and exact scenario bytes were reused; only guidance/scenario paths were substituted. Rubric, earlier results, score counts and this report were never supplied to respondents. All complete final responses were manually read and scored claim by claim; evidence quotations are retained per claim in `scores.json`.
+
+AFTER launch order was A1/B1/C1, A2/B2/C2, A3/B3/C3, A4/B4/C4, A5/B5/C5, with at most three active respondents, as parent explicitly authorized. The prepared pack specified one active test child, matching baseline execution; this concurrency difference is recorded rather than hidden. There were no cross-respondent messages or shared respondent writes.
+
+Source was frozen before the first respondent at commit **`0bb280edcf5fc6a60499fdfdb090d1819a432963`** from:
+
+`/Users/alepar/.aisw/profiles/codex/codex-3/worktrees/02a7/superpowers/.worktrees/super-auto-workflow-reliability--task-super-plan-ufz.6`
+
+All selected files equaled their committed bytes at freeze. `source-manifest.json` records original absolute paths, repository paths, commit, exact inclusive line ranges, full-file SHA-256, excerpt SHA-256 and full-file snapshot path. `guidance-A.txt`, `guidance-B.txt`, `guidance-C.txt` preserve exact delivered references. `frozen-artifact-hashes.json` records pretrial frozen hashes. Posttrial `source-recheck.json` confirms every selected full-file and excerpt hash still matches.
+
+Selection preserves the baseline’s logical operative sections and whole clauses. Expanded new contracts include verification-only selection in the full task reviewer; adjacent bundle identity before worktree topology; the final-review/continuity/collection contracts surrounding Phase 6; task-base/run-baseline attribution; the expanded whole upstream Process; and updated output process tags. The broader reference is actual committed product text, not proposed wording. Exact selection is a visible experimental input, and comparison does not isolate any single sentence’s causal effect.
+
+Invalidate applicability to a later source state if any relevant selected file or required referenced contract changes. A parent can recompute the full/excerpt hashes in `source-manifest.json`; the complete source snapshots permit review even if the worktree moves. Changes only to tests do not by themselves change the frozen guidance bytes.
+
+The tested input is an excerpt pack, not automatic skill discovery or a complete end-to-end harness session. Both historical arms inherited shared system/developer context and skill catalog; “no guidance” means absence of the tested workflow references, not a blank-system control. Scoring is manual and unblinded; n=5 per scenario is small. Historical controls were not rerun concurrently with AFTER. Text answers cannot establish actual process cleanup, isolation, persistence, schema/helper correctness, source-bound check execution, or production failure rates. Independent deterministic/mechanical and live workflow checks remain separate evidence.
+
+## Artifacts
+
+All artifacts are under **`/private/tmp/ufz-after-behavior/`**:
+
+- `report.md`: this report.
+- `source-manifest.json`, `freeze-metadata.json`, `frozen-artifact-hashes.json`, `source-recheck.json`: source identities, protocol details, initial hashes and posttrial recheck.
+- `source-snapshot/`: full exact source files underlying every excerpt.
+- `guidance-{A,B,C}.txt`, `scenario-{A,B,C}.txt`: exact delivered references and unchanged cases.
+- `{A,B,C}-after-{1,2,3,4,5}-prompt.txt` and corresponding `-response.txt`: every complete submitted prompt and final answer.
+- `trials.json`: every respondent’s canonical agent identity, completion/counting status and artifact paths.
+- `scores.json`, `claim-summary.json`: private rubric application with per-claim quotations, dispositions, omissions/ambiguities and baseline comparison.
+- `baseline-reference/`: full frozen original pack including all 30 baseline prompts/responses, original scores, source manifest, pilot attempt/exclusion evidence and original report. Original absolute `/tmp/workflow-reliability-baseline/` paths remain in archived historical artifacts; local basenames provide the preserved bytes.
+- `freeze.py`, `score.py`: freeze and score assembly scripts. Scoring decisions are explicit manual judgments; quotation selection is not a score classifier.
+- `artifact-hashes.json`: final portable artifact SHA-256 inventory.
+
+No product source, project tracker, Git state or Herdr membership/messages were mutated by this evaluator or its respondents.
