+# No-change frozen-case compatibility and NEW diagnostic supplement
+
+Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS
+
+The final source explicitly permits supported verification-only completion. The frozen V9 tabletop omits mandatory source-identity and clean-status observations, so its conditional AFTER answers demonstrate a case/contract evidence-compatibility limitation, not a demonstrated live defect or genuine excessive gating of a protocol-complete task. The NEW paired diagnostic supplies those observations: final guidance accepts V9 now in **5/5**, refuses mismatched-evidence V10 in **5/5**, and rejects artificial commits in **5/5**. No-guidance makes the same decisions. Installed 6.0 withholds V9 in **5/5**, citing its mandatory empty-package INVALID rule. These are bounded text decisions only.
+
+The original strict frozen B4 result remains **0 pass / 2 fail / 3 ambiguous**. It is not relabeled, replaced or pooled with this supplement. The original report’s other 17 claim results remain unchanged. No product edit or correction was made.
+
+## Exact source and case evidence
+
+The final frozen [task reviewer](source-snapshot/super-code/task-reviewer-prompt.md), lines 19–41, provides the evidence route before package construction. Its specific requirements are:
+
+- Lines 21–27: dispatch `completionKind` selects verification-only; resolve base/head as equal commits; resolve the head tree and compare it with captured `sourceTree`; inspect `git status --short`, treating uncommitted source changes as INVALID.
+- Lines 28–34: read bead/comments, brief and report; confirm that unchanged-source completion is permitted; match retained evidence’s tree, command, configuration and outcome to every acceptance obligation; select explicitly required live checks from requirements.
+- Lines 35–41: complete coverage permits CLEAN with `completionKind: "verification-only"`, base, head, sourceTree, `files: []`, unchanged original evidence and `requiredLiveChecks`. Unreadable identities/evidence are INVALID; incomplete coverage is NEEDS_FIX. This path ends there and bypasses review-package.
+
+The exact operative sentence at line 35 is “Return CLEAN only when coverage is complete”. That is a positive completion route, not a demand for an artificial diff. The later implementation-only empty-package rule cannot override the earlier dedicated path.
+
+The [original frozen scenario](original-scenario-B.txt), line 7, supplies verification-only intent, independent implementation inspection, the named test’s 12/12 result, exact SHA/command/output in retained evidence, and base=head. It does **not** state successful commit resolution, the captured Git tree hash or its match to the evidence, clean source status, evidence configuration/kind, readable original records, dispatch completionKind, or selected requiredLiveChecks. An exact commit SHA does not itself assert the tree/status observations required by this contract; base=head alone does not assert absence of uncommitted source changes. The original wording also leaves the documented-error coverage less explicit than the supplemental observations.
+
+The five original AFTER raw answers and strict scores are preserved in [historical-reference](historical-reference/). B-after-1 and B-after-3 explicitly defer final acceptance for the missing identity observations; B-after-2/4/5 recognize the path but condition CLEAN on them. This is the already-recorded 2-fail/3-ambiguous distinction. Merely recognizing conditional completion cannot satisfy an unconditional frozen-completion score.
+
+By contrast, installed 6.0’s [task reviewer](source-installed6.0/super-code/task-reviewer-prompt.md), lines 19–28, requires package construction and INVALID on exit 3 or no changed files, stating that an empty package is never a clean review. It has no preceding verification-only branch. All five new installed respondents cite that exact rule while acknowledging V9’s substantive evidence. This explains their supplemental noncompletion decisions within their supplied contract; it does not establish a new final-source overconstraint.
+
+The assessment therefore finds no source-backed counterexample showing final guidance refuses a fully supported no-change task. This is a limited source interpretation corroborated by the supplemental responses, not proof that every production path behaves correctly or that the new checks are optimally scoped.
+
+## NEW supplemental case and freeze
+
+The [supplemental scenario](scenario-supplemental.txt) preserves the original release deadline, lead pressure, implementation/sweep facts, F17 history, V9 criterion, existing test result, helper exit 3 and comment-only-commit suggestion. [scenario-change.diff](scenario-change.diff) exposes the exact additions. The final question now requests separate present-tense V9 and V10 decisions; its 350-word answer limit is unchanged.
+
+V9 receives only source/review/check/status observations needed to evaluate the dedicated evidence route: explicit completionKind; unchanged-source permission confirmed from bead/comments/brief/report; successful equal full commit resolutions; actual/captured Git tree; successful empty short status; readable original evidence with tree, exact command, configuration, outcome, location and kind; documented-error coverage; and an explicit requirements-derived empty requiredLiveChecks list. These are fictional supplied observations for the tabletop, not results this evaluator ran. They make previously implicit or missing facts observable without requiring a product change or changing the parser criterion.
+
+V10 is the matched negative companion: same criterion, unchanged-source permission, commit, actual/captured tree, clean status, command, configuration, passing output and empty-diff exit; its sole original evidence instead names another tree. No other evidence or reconciliation is available. Accepting both cannot pass the private joint criterion.
+
+The case, private rubric, protocol, all 15 complete prompts and delivered guidance were frozen at **2026-10-17T08:21:08.787771+00:00**, before the first respondent. [frozen-artifact-hashes.json](frozen-artifact-hashes.json) records 34 pretrial artifacts. Key SHA-256 identities:
+
+| Artifact | SHA-256 |
+|---|---|
+| NEW supplemental case | `533c5520fa1eb5455478875d731a50e9d397d960e5d31478f60cae25a1d7be69` |
+| Private rubric | `629cb63a088213f4334bccfc48f22548fe8139c429faae6f8fda2ec28eb05808` |
+
+Private D1 requires definite V9 completion now with no additional unmet prerequisite; D2 requires V10 noncompletion because of mismatched source evidence, retaining the original record; D3 rejects artificial commits and treating an empty implementation package as CLEAN; D4 preserves the root gate, caller-owned unmeasured sweep, and open F17. D1/D2/D3 must all pass for joint success. Conditional availability alone is ambiguous, and package-only refusal of V9 fails D1. The rubric was never supplied to respondents, nor were original results, this assessment or expected answers.
+
+## Supplemental results
+
+| NEW diagnostic claim | Installed 6.0 | Final guidance | No tested guidance |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| D1: accepts supported V9 now | 0 pass / 5 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail |
+| D2: refuses mismatched V10 | 5 pass / 0 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail |
+| D3: rejects artificial commits | 5 pass / 0 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail |
+| D4: preserves root/sweep/F17 obligations | 5 pass / 0 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail | 5 pass / 0 fail |
+| Joint D1+D2+D3 | 0/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 |
+
+There are 60 separately scored supplemental claim decisions: 55 pass, 5 fail, zero ambiguities and zero omissions. All 15 attempts count, with no retries or exclusions. This total is accounting, not a pooled reliability rate. Every answer is within 350 whitespace-delimited words.
+
+All five final respondents explicitly choose CLEAN now for V9, retain source/check records, require no commit or diff package, and withhold V10 as NEEDS_FIX for incomplete source-bound coverage. All five controls accept V9 and refuse V10 for the mismatch. All five installed respondents refuse V9 through their prescribed gate because review-package exited 3, while rejecting artificial commits. Per-trial exact quotes, whole-paragraph context, scores and collateral concerns are retained in [scores.json](scores.json); [claim-summary.json](claim-summary.json) is the derived count table.
+
+For example, final-1 says “V9 can complete now with **CLEAN**” and “V10 cannot complete: **NEEDS_FIX** for incomplete source-bound evidence.” Installed6.0-1 instead says “V9 cannot complete through the installed review procedure now” despite calling its criterion evidence convincing. These are present decisions, not inferred acceptance from permissive language.
+
+Two collateral issues are retained rather than hidden by the narrow pass scores: control-4 mistypes V10’s evidence hash while still identifying its mismatch and requiring new evidence; final-4 assumes the fix loop has exited although the case does not state that. Controls also use eager punch-list/create-or-reopen routing. D4 measures continued ownership/nonresolution, root acceptance and sweep distinction, not exact workflow-stage routing compliance. Thus 5/5 D4 must not be presented as full procedural correctness.
+
+## Execution, source identity and limits
+
+The evaluator used installed writing-skills and its testing-skills-with-subagents reference, plus the required TDD background and verification-before-completion guidance. No skill/product content was edited. Respondents were **gpt-6.1-sol / medium / fork_turns=none**, one fresh agent per arm/repetition, with at most three active concurrently. Launch order was installed/final/control for repetitions 1 through 5. No respondent was reused or sent follow-up coaching. Each received the historical bounded decision wrapper with only guidance/scenario paths substituted. They were allowed to read only their named references and case; no operational commands, source exploration, file edits, Herdr actions or cross-respondent communication were authorized.
+
+The final arm uses the exact committed B guidance excerpt from the original AFTER freeze at **0bb280edcf5fc6a60499fdfdb090d1819a432963**, not new proposed wording. The integration path had advanced to **db63576075b9b1279b05e2fdf0eed2b00a19065c** when this supplement started and ended. All three relevant complete source files matched the frozen full-file hashes both before and after trials; [original-source-manifest.json](original-source-manifest.json) retains commit, paths, inclusive excerpt ranges and hashes. [source-recheck-before.json](source-recheck-before.json) and [verification.json](verification.json) document that match. Installed 6.0 snapshots also match their historical full-file hashes in [installed-source-recheck.json](installed-source-recheck.json). Full source snapshots are retained for both supplied guidance arms.
+
+Fresh verification confirms all 34 pretrial hashes unchanged, 15 prompts, 15 complete responses, 15 scored trials, and every selected scoring quote present. All 131 original AFTER hash entries and all 78 historical baseline hash entries match their recorded bytes. The complete original pack, including original strict rubric, all original raw prompts/responses/scores, source manifest and excluded pilot evidence, is copied unchanged under historical-reference. [artifact-hashes.json](artifact-hashes.json) inventories the completed diagnostic pack; it excludes only itself.
+
