+# Promotion review disposition
+
+Fresh same-family reviewer reliability_promotion recommended SPLIT for .4 and .5, PROMOTE for .8, LEAF for the remaining tasks.
+
+Applied .4 split: .4 owns durable recovery/fix records; .12 owns resume reconciliation, depending on .4. Existing .6/.7/.9 consumers keep their edges to .4 because they consume records, not resume behavior.
+
+Applied .5 split: .5 owns evidence records; .13 owns no-change completion, depending on .5. Existing .6/.7 consumers keep their edges to .5 because they consume evidence, not no-change completion.
+
+Applied .8 promotion: finding continuity requires nested contract design, including external roast-ledger ownership and supported disposition. It is an epic with sp:needs-design, sp_depth=1, sp_order=1. No nested work starts before the interactive top-split gate.
+
+The remaining leaves retain their reviewed scopes; no decomposition override. Root integration sweep is created after coverage as required by super-design.
