++  - super-plan-ufz.1 · Pin review inputs and isolate mutable reproductions · Bind review source and diff inputs to captured commit identities. · deps: none
++      owns: Stable review source identities and review-owned mutable reproduction resources.
++      consumes: Existing Git revision and worktree ownership conventions; existing review dispatch inputs.
++  - super-plan-ufz.2 · Propagate cleanup uncertainty and retain needed resources · Carry verified stopped, surviving, unknown and deliberately kept outcomes through existing process/worktree helpers, coordinator Finish, ordinary-subagent instr · deps: none
++      owns: Cleanup outcome meaning, resource retention and truthful propagation to finish/report consumers.
++      consumes: Existing run/task ownership boundaries and process-root matching.
++  - super-plan-ufz.3 · Recheck admission and refresh external dependency readiness · Within the existing scheduler, recheck hold/cancellation/dependency admission after acquiring capacity and before dispatch. · deps: none
++      owns: Post-capacity admission, external dependency satisfaction and bounded in-flight readiness refresh.
++      consumes: Existing scheduler slots, tracker observations and task/review associations.
++  - super-plan-ufz.4 · Persist recovery obligations and fix history records · Extend existing ledger/run artifacts only for missing holds, pending closures, deferred obligations and relevant fix history. · deps: none
++      owns: Durable recovery/fix records and compatible digest transport.
++      consumes: Existing ledger identity, task branch landing evidence, tracker closure observations and run artifacts.
++  - super-plan-ufz.5 · Record source-bound evidence and check outcomes · Extend existing evidence records only for missing source tree, command/configuration, result, location and kind. · deps: none
++      owns: Source-bound evidence identity, kind and check outcomes.
++      consumes: Existing task acceptance criteria, implementation/review dispatch and source-tree identities.
++  - super-plan-ufz.6 · Keep super-auto root acceptance caller-owned · Keep deferred sweeps as caller-owned measurement obligations while code findings remain actionable. · deps: super-plan-ufz.4, super-plan-ufz.5, super-plan-ufz.8.3
++      owns: Caller-owned deferred measurement and super-auto root acceptance gates.
