++    "description": "Keep deferred sweeps as caller-owned measurement obligations while code findings remain actionable. Under super-auto, prevent root closure before required reviews, measurements and human gates; preserve standalone acceptance ownership. Verification consumes recovery obligations, task evidence and outstanding invocation findings from the named prerequisites. The coordinator owns fresh-agent acceptance scenarios; the implementer owns deterministic gate and status fixtures.\n\nSpec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability-design.md\nFiles: skills/super-auto/SKILL.md, skills/super-auto/run-state.md, skills/super-auto/resume.md, skills/super-auto/scripts/report-status, skills/super-code/scripts/close-in-tree-epics, skills/super-code/coordinator.js, skills/super-code/coordinator-workflow.md, skills/super-code/coordinator-subagents.md, tests/super-code/replay-harness.mjs, tests/super-auto/test-scripts.sh, tests/super-auto/test-contract-lint.sh\nowns: Caller-owned deferred measurement and super-auto root acceptance gates.\nconsumes: Recovery obligations from super-plan-ufz.4; evidence outcomes from super-plan-ufz.5; outstanding invocation findings from super-plan-ufz.8.3; existing super-auto final sweep and human gates.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] A deferred sweep remains an explicit pending measurement with an owner and does not hide actual code findings (needs: super-plan-ufz.4, super-plan-ufz.5).\n- [ ] All implementation leaves can finish while the super-auto root remains open for required review, measurement or human acceptance (needs: super-plan-ufz.4, super-plan-ufz.5, super-plan-ufz.8.3).\n- [ ] Standalone callers retain their existing acceptance ownership.\n- [ ] Deterministic gate/status fixtures pass; the coordinator owns fresh-agent deferred-sweep and final-acceptance scenarios.\nblocked-by super-plan-ufz.4: consumes Durable recovery facts, compatible digest transport and resume reconciliation of those facts.\nblocked-by super-plan