++    "description": "Within the existing scheduler, recheck hold/cancellation/dependency admission after acquiring capacity and before dispatch. Distinguish local implementation readiness from tracker review/blocker/human-gate closure. Refresh external readiness at bounded opportunities while work is in flight. A failed lookup holds only affected work. Exercise both Workflow mechanics and ordinary-subagent contract; the coordinator owns live ordinary-subagent evaluation.\n\nSpec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability-design.md\nFiles: skills/super-code/coordinator.js, skills/super-code/coordinator-workflow.md, skills/super-code/coordinator-subagents.md, tests/super-code/replay-harness.mjs\nowns: Post-capacity admission, external dependency satisfaction and bounded in-flight readiness refresh.\nconsumes: Existing scheduler slots, tracker observations and task/review associations.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] A hold established during a slot wait prevents dispatch; the slot is released and no implementation attempt is falsely reported.\n- [ ] A closed external review dependency releases its consumer even when its ID is absent from implementation completion sets.\n- [ ] An external release becomes visible while a long-running task remains in flight.\n- [ ] A failed dependency lookup keeps affected work held with a reason while unrelated eligible work continues.\n- [ ] Deterministic Workflow replay covers both execution-path contracts; coordinator-owned live evaluation checks changed ordinary-subagent instructions.",
