++    "title": "Correct profiler availability bounds and bottleneck claims",
++    "description": "Keep creation, mapping readiness and dependency readiness distinct in the existing profiler. Bound waits by evidenced availability, keep unknown timestamps unknown and label invocation/residual graph scope. Include planning time in bottleneck diagnosis, label modeled improvements as estimates and separate all-agent from task-slot concurrency. Settle existing profile generation ownership after each settled invocation and append/copy output once. The coordinator owns any fresh-agent interpretation evaluation.\n\nSpec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability-design.md\nFiles: skills/super-code/scripts/run-profile.mjs, skills/super-code/coordinator-workflow.md, skills/super-code/coordinator-subagents.md, skills/super-auto/SKILL.md, skills/super-auto/report-prompt.md, tests/super-code/run-profile-fixture.mjs, tests/super-code/run-profile-ordinary-fixture.mjs, tests/super-code/test-run-profile.sh, tests/super-code/test-run-profile-in-flight.sh\nowns: Profiler availability/timing semantics, planning-aware diagnosis, graph/concurrency labels and profile-generation handoff.\nconsumes: Existing journal/transcript/ordinary-subagent tracker evidence and settled invocation output paths.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] A late-created task is never assigned wait time before its creation; unavailable timestamps remain unknown.\n- [ ] Creation, mapping-ready and dependency-ready evidence retain their actual meanings throughout waits and schedule estimates.\n- [ ] A planning-dominated timeline does not claim task parallelism alone removes the bottleneck; counterfactuals are labeled estimates.\n- [ ] Graph labels describe observed invocation/residual scope without inventing historical topology, and all-agent/task-slot concurrency have separate labels.\n- [ ] Profiles are generated after settled invocations by a named owner, then appended and copied without contradictory Finish/caller ownership.\n- [ ] Workflow and ordinary-subagent deterministic profiler fix