++    "title": "Preserve invocation findings until supported disposition",
++    "description": "Give super-code invocation review artifacts unique identities and retain unresolved findings across blocked/retried invocations. Make the punch list an outstanding-deferred view whose resolution requires evidence, including fixes supplied elsewhere. Preserve uncertain matches separately. Consume the parallel roast-redesign team's ledger contract; do not build a replacement roast ledger, redesign triggers or amend workflow. Explicit overlap to settle: that team's vision currently dissolves a finding on later silence, contrary to this approved invariant. The coordinator owns cross-run/agent behavior evaluation.\n\nSpec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability-design.md\nFiles: skills/super-code/coordinator.js, skills/super-code/scripts/dispatch-text.mjs, skills/super-code/scripts/report-verdict, skills/super-auto/SKILL.md, skills/super-auto/run-state.md, skills/super-auto/resume.md, skills/super-auto/scripts/scope-dispositions, skills/super-auto/report-prompt.md, tests/super-code/test-report-verdict.sh, tests/super-code/test-dispatch-text.sh, tests/super-auto/test-scripts.sh\nowns: Immutable super-code invocation reviews, outstanding invocation-finding consumption and evidence-backed punch-list disposition.\nconsumes: Existing finding/task records and review extraction; the roast-redesign team's externally owned ledger interface when available.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] A blocked review followed by a silent retry preserves the earlier unresolved finding and its source artifact.\n- [ ] A deferred item fixed by another task leaves the punch list only after supported verification.\n- [ ] A fix task's success claim or a later review's silence alone cannot resolve a prior actionable finding.\n- [ ] Explicit references link repeated appearances; uncertain matches remain separate pending judgment, and rejected findings retain reasoning/evidence.\n- [ ] No competing roast ledger, trigger policy or amend workflow is introduced; the external ledger consumer seam is checked against the continuity invariant.\n- [ ] Deterministic artifact/disposition fixtures pass; the coordinator owns fresh-agent interrupted-invocation evaluation.\nNested spec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability/2026-10-16-finding-continuity-design.md\nDesign complete: no new abstractions; four reviewed LEAF children. Core contract independent of external ledger API; silence cannot resolve.\n",
